  "description": "<p>Piedmont Virginia Community College is a public community college in Charlottesville, Virginia. It was founded in 1972. The highest degree offered at Piedmont Virginia Community College is an associate degree and courses last for two years. Interestingly, the school has an open admissions policy and offers credit for life experiences.</p> <p>Piedmont Virginia Community College (PVCC) offers students modern classrooms and labs with up-to-date technology and equipment. PVCC's Eugene Giuseppe Center for Visual Arts has state-of-the-art studios for art and design students. At the same time, the Main Stage Theatre hosts a variety of performances and events throughout the year. The college also provides a library with a vast collection of books and study spaces to ensure students can access necessary resources on campus. There is also a fitness center and athletic fields for student recreation and wellness. PVCC's Student Services office provides various student resources and support services, including academic advice, counseling, career services, and disability support.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Community is a big part of campus life, offering a sense of belonging to college students looking to meet like-minded peers and develop personally and academically. Particularly active students can benefit from the number of student activities taking place on campus, as well as free events situated locally throughout the year. The Panther Fitness Center contains two rooms fully equipped with equipment for student use, and there is an activity calendar of PVCC events for students to attend. Volunteer experiences and art exhibitions are free ways students can enhance their well-being and have fun amongst their age group while making the most of their college experience.</p>",
