      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Piedmont Virginia Community College is a public community college in Charlottesville, Virginia. It was founded in 1972. The highest degree offered at Piedmont Virginia Community College is an associate degree and courses last for two years. Interestingly, the school has an open admissions policy and offers credit for life experiences.</p><p>PVCC's Eugene Giuseppe Center for Visual Arts has state-of-the-art studios for art and design students. At the same time, the Main Stage Theatre hosts a variety of performances and events throughout the year. PVCC's Student Services office provides various student resources and support services, including academic advice, counseling, career services, and disability support.</p>",
